From 3960d507e971a20f5e357b6b8539dd958538a0cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ritesh Pandit <riteshp2001@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 13:27:16 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 137/140] feat(gestures): make nested tab swipes configurable

- Add a persistent nested_tab_swipes_enabled preference, defaulting to true
  to preserve the currently enabled inner-tab gestures.
- Expose Swipe between inner tabs in Settings > Gestures beside the existing
  media-item swipe settings, using the standard switch and preference divider.
- Gate opted-in nested pagers in the shared NavigationPager with the live
  preference. Music, Network, and Recents respond without an app restart.
- Keep main navigation, tab taps, item swipe actions, and other nested pager
  defaults unchanged. Disabled nested pagers retain the pass-through scroll
  connection instead of consuming parent navigation gestures.
- Register a settings-search target with nested/inner/tab/navigation keywords.
- Translate the title and summary in the default resources and all nine
  existing non-English locales.

Validation: focused editor diagnostics, source/call-site review, XML parsing
and unique-key checks across all ten resource sets, and git diff --check.
No build, tests, emulator, or device gesture checks were run under the standing
static-only constraint. No generated schemas or changelog files were edited.
